From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 23:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cix: pick the hdmi-codec child explicitly, not any child

cix_acpi_dp_audio_get_codec_name() locates the DP platform device from its
ACPI handle and then calls device_find_any_child() to find the HDMI audio
codec beneath it. That returns an arbitrary child.

On Radxa Orion O6N running 7.2, each DP device has several children:

  CIXH502F:00 -> consumer:platform:CIXH5010:00   (fw_devlink)
                 hdmi-audio-codec.15.auto        (the actual codec)
                 i2c-4
                 supplier:platform:CIXHA010:00   (fw_devlink)

plus a wakeup source. device_find_any_child() picks one of the others, so
the machine driver ends up asking snd_soc for codecs that do not exist:

  sky1-asoc-card CIXH6070:00: num_links = 3
  sky1-asoc-card CIXH6070:00: dp[0]:cpu[CIXH6011:02][i2s-mc-aif1] \
      codec[wakeup100][i2s-hifi] platform[CIXH6011:02]
  sky1-asoc-card CIXH6070:00: dp[1]:... codec[wakeup101][i2s-hifi] ...
  sky1-asoc-card CIXH6070:00: dp[4]:... codec[wakeup102][i2s-hifi] ...

No dai_link ever binds, so no card registers at all: /proc/asound/cards
reports "no soundcards" and /dev/snd contains only seq and timer.

7.0.12 was unaffected by luck rather than by design - the DP device had
fewer children there (display was not probing and the fw_devlink
consumer/supplier link devices were absent), so the arbitrary child
happened to be the codec.

Match the codec explicitly by its platform driver name instead.
dev_name() remains correct once the right child is selected: the hdmi-codec
ASoC component registers under the device name (hdmi-audio-codec.N.auto),
which is what snd_soc compares dai_link codecs->name against.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c b/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c
--- a/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c	2026-07-21 23:24:50.331047488 +0800
+++ b/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c	2026-07-21 23:24:50.331699741 +0800
@@ -3,9 +3,11 @@
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/syscon.h>
+#include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include "card-utils.h"
 #include <sound/jack.h>
+#include <sound/hdmi-codec.h>
 
 #define SKY1_AUDSS_CRU_INFO_MCLK		0x70
 #define SKY1_AUDSS_CRU_INFO_MCLK_DIV_OFF(x)	(10 + (3 * (x)))
@@ -803,6 +805,19 @@
 	return dev_name(&adev->dev);
 }
 
+/*
+ * A DP device has several children: the hdmi-codec platform device, an i2c
+ * adapter, and fw_devlink consumer:/supplier: link devices (plus a wakeup
+ * source). device_find_any_child() returns an arbitrary one, so match the
+ * hdmi-codec explicitly by its platform driver name.
+ */
+static int cix_dp_match_hdmi_codec(struct device *dev, const void *data)
+{
+	return dev->bus == &platform_bus_type &&
+	       to_platform_device(dev)->name &&
+	       !strcmp(to_platform_device(dev)->name, HDMI_CODEC_DRV_NAME);
+}
+
 static const char *cix_acpi_dp_audio_get_codec_name(int idx)
 {
 	struct acpi_device *adev;
@@ -824,10 +839,15 @@
 	if (!dev)
 		return NULL;
 
-	dpdev = device_find_any_child(dev);
+	dpdev = device_find_child(dev, NULL, cix_dp_match_hdmi_codec);
 	if (!dpdev)
 		return NULL;
 
+	/*
+	 * dev_name() is correct here: the hdmi-codec ASoC component is
+	 * registered under the device name (hdmi-audio-codec.N.auto), which is
+	 * what snd_soc matches dai_link codecs->name against.
+	 */
 	return dev_name(dpdev);
 }
 
